  "domain": "blockchain",
  "definition": "BIP-341 is the Bitcoin Improvement Proposal that defines the Taproot upgrade, introducing Pay-to-Taproot (P2TR) as a new output type that merges script and key-path spending under a unified commitment scheme. It combines Schnorr signatures with Merklised Abstract Syntax Trees (MAST) to allow complex spending conditions to be committed on-chain while only revealing the executed branch at spend time. The proposal activated on the Bitcoin mainnet in November 2021 at block height 709,632. BIP-341 is accompanied by BIP-340 (Schnorr signatures) and BIP-342 (Tapscript), forming the complete Taproot bundle. The upgrade significantly improves privacy, fungibility, and script expressiveness for Bitcoin.",
